A||N||1||86_Fastback||Mini-van 3.4l and Fiero||||5||
Z||000000||86_Fastback||10-30-2000||08:52 AM||||I am looking at doing a 3.4l swap into my 86 Fiero GT.  Like many, I want the most for my money.  Does anyone know if it is possible to use the Fiero ECU with the 3.4L out of the mini-van?  I would like to keep the aluminum heads and the intake rather than using the fiero's mainly because everything would need to be stripped and painted.<P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||10-30-2000||05:49 PM||||There has been a lot of discussion on this same topic. You might want to search for "3.4". Should be several days of entertainment.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Having said that, I believe that you will have to retain the minivan ECM, too. The newer 3.4's are DIS. The Fiero ECM is looking for a distributor. I've heard that the ECM could be adapted, and that the wires could be spliced. I have my reservations about this. Never seen it done. Won't believe it until I do. Another option <I>might</I> be to use the intake plenum off of a later Z-24, if there was one available with the aluminum heads <I>and</I> a distributor. Heard rumors of that one, too.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>"If I have to fake 'genuine concern' one more time today, I'm gonna scream!" -TCH||||reg||1
